{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792935250,"nonce":"pKMJDTZN9AHp3CUoThLAq1l1ccs=","title":"The project format RayDE opens: cbproj for tools and IDEs","message":"RayDE (rayzor-blade/RayDE, the Haxe IDE on ashui) opens, edits, builds, runs\nand serves Caribou projects. The `.cbproj` file is the project, and caribou\nanswers the questions an IDE asks of it, so that RayDE never re-derives\ncaribou's rules. The format was agreed with the RayDE sessions (rayde-f5,\nrayde-0f) on 2026-10-25.\n\n\nRayDE's ProjectFile reads a project into these fields:\n- a kind: folder, hxml, haxelib or rayzor;\n- a root, name, runtime, runnable and main;\n- the Haxe compiler arguments its compilation server uses for diagnostics,\n  completion and the Run build.\n\nrayzor.toml's `[build] class-paths` and `defines` become `-cp` and `-D`. A\nsettings form has one card per manifest table and saves straight to the\nmanifest. Run and Build are the only configurations, and a project runs\nthrough a CLI whose stdout and stderr are streamed. A `.cbproj` becomes a\nfifth project kind.\n\n\n- **Haxe class paths and defines**: `[haxe] class-paths`, `defines`, with\n  rayzor.toml's keys. The source roots are compiled whole; the extra class\n  paths are compiled only as far as the program reaches.\n- **The resolved project**: `caribou project --json`, including the exact\n  haxe arguments.\n- **Workspaces**: `[workspace] members`, mirroring rayzor's.\n- **Diagnostics**: one JSON object per line on stderr with `--diagnostics\n  json` (git-bug f570765965bed74b0f2abdb161479905c4ea3330fd9035bb89257f3547d3262d).\n- **Run settings**: `[run] preset` and `args`. `caribou serve` prints its URL\n  as its first JSON line.\n- **New projects**: `caribou new` scaffolds one, and RayDE's starter runs it.\n\nThe language server is the caribou lsp epic\n(1626b90d930d209e848220743e00494408af449d2cdabdddea70f6c0a5337545).\nUntil it lands, RayDE's compilation server uses `haxe.args`.","files":null}]}